[h1]Timber! Chainsaw[/h1]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer[/b]

A working gasoline chainsaw: start it, fell trees in seconds, carve through zombies, refuel it with petrol... and mind the noise.

[h2]Inspired by Chainsaw B42[/h2]

This mod is inspired by [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692027888]Chainsaw B42[/url] by Likit and remade from scratch with the same features: new code, sounds, poster and icons, plus the improvements listed below.

It uses the same item names as Chainsaw B42: in a save made with Chainsaw B42, your chainsaws keep their fuel. [b]Do not enable both mods at the same time.[/b]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]

[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3694097672]TooltipLib[/url]
[/list]

[b]Compatibility:[/b] If you use Better Item Info (EURY_ITEMINFO), load it before Timber! Chainsaw to avoid the reported missing Vorpal weapon tooltips. Better Item Info is optional. Restart the game completely after changing the order.

[b]Weight and condition:[/b] Weight: 7, engine on or off. Maximum condition: 127, to prevent damaged chainsaws suddenly breaking when unequipped or reloaded. Wear settings are unchanged: durability is about 37% lower than with the old maximum of 200.

[h2]How to use[/h2]

[list]
[*]Right-click the chainsaw: [b]Start the chainsaw[/b]. It goes in both hands and needs fuel. A worn chainsaw may refuse to start.
[*]Hold the attack button (left click): the chainsaw stays pointed forward at full throttle and cuts whatever is in front of you, zombies or trees.
[*]Trees: right-click a tree, [b]Cut down the tree with the chainsaw[/b]. A small tree falls in 1 to 3 seconds, the biggest in about 11 seconds.
[*][b]Stop the chainsaw[/b], then [b]Refuel the chainsaw[/b] with a container of pure petrol.
[*]The tooltip shows the engine state and the fuel.
[/list]

[h2]Improvements over the original[/h2]

[list]
[*]Trees really fall (they only lost 1 point per hit). Cutting wood burns more fuel than idling.
[*]Refuelling takes only the litres the tank needs, and only petrol (it emptied the whole container, whatever its liquid).
[*]The fuel consumption, noise, damage and loot options are applied.
[*]No more errors when looking at a liquid container (water dispenser, bottles...).
[*]The chainsaw sounds follow the Sound effects volume, and each one can be set in Options > Audio > Advanced.
[*]A broken chainsaw stays broken until you repair it; the repair keeps the fuel, with no limit on repairs.
[*]Found in logging sites, ranger stations, fire stations, barns and garages.
[/list]

[h2]Multiplayer[/h2]

The server decides everything: start and stop, fuel, wear, fallen trees. The engine stops when the chainsaw leaves your hands, runs dry, breaks, or when you get in a vehicle. Nearby players hear your engine running.

[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]

Fuel consumption, damage, combat wear, tree cutting wear, cutting speed, noise radius, starting failures, loot.

[h2]Support the project[/h2]

Enjoying the mod? A coffee helps fund new features and translations.
